  "content": "Ethan Park putts best on the team by strokes gained putting. He's at -1.92 strokes per round over his last eight rounds, which is every round in his newest-ten window. Owen Carter is next at -2.06 over his last eight rounds.\n\nCarter has the fewest putts per round at 31.88 over those eight rounds. Tyler Hayes is next at 32.29 over seven rounds, and Park is third at 32.5 over eight. So Park and Carter are close, and which one is better depends on the measure.\n\nBoth are still losing strokes to the baseline. The team's pooled figure is -3.03 over 55 rounds from seven players. The Tour baseline in these reads is 0 (PGA Tour 2024). There is no college figure for strokes gained, so I can't give a division comparison. Jackson Hale is lowest on the team at -4.77 over eight rounds.\n\nAudit Testplayer has no recorded rounds, so he isn't in the ranking. The newest rounds in these windows end between late September and October 21, so this doesn't include anything more recent.",
